!data/results/halo_memory_*.json
# regenerated by the README golden path (experiments/cycle2568_starving_philosopher.py); not tracked
data/figures/cycle2568_starving_philosopher.png

# HALO pre-registered memory test: the raw 32^3 density meshes are ~190 MB for the
# 60-run grid and are regenerable bit for bit from the seeds, because a run is
# reproducible tick for tick (tests/halo/memory_prereg_grid.sh). The per-run JSON,
# the derived analysis and the verdict are committed; the meshes are not.
data/results/halo/memory_prereg/*.mesh.f32
# The voided grid's meshes were NOT covered by the line above, so a `git add` of the
# results tree would have published 73 MB of runs that are void by their own record
# (all 23 log `console: Failed to load resource: net::ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND`). They are
# kept locally because they are the bit-exact replication evidence for the instrument,
# and their JSONs are small enough to commit; the meshes are not.
data/results/halo/memory_prereg_voided/*.mesh.f32
